{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-heavy-atom-examples-table5-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table5-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 5 from tm-heavy-atom-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-heavy-atom-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-heavy-atom-examples-table5-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table5-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Data table 5 from tm-heavy-atom-examples</em></p>\n<p>This data table supports the Cobalt-60 example (Example 7,\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{60}\\mathrm{Co} \\to {}^{60}\\mathrm{Ni}</code> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta^-</code> decay) in\n<a href=\"#sec:tm-heavy-atom-examples\">Heavy-atom worked examples</a>, where it is the\ninput to the shell-correction step.  Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(n)</code> is the torus-knot Markov trace\nat outer-shell occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> (the transfer weight for that shell), and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\log_q \\tau(n)</code> is its base-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> logarithm.  The two upper rows are the\nparent <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{60}\\mathrm{Co}</code> outer shells (proton occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 7</code>,\nneutron occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 5</code>); the two lower rows are the daughter\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{60}\\mathrm{Ni}</code> outer shells (proton occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 8</code>, a closed\nshell, and neutron occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 4</code>).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Occupancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(n)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\log_q \\tau(n)</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">7</code> (parent proton)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 1.299</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+2.51</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code> (parent neutron)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 0.993</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.07</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8</code> (daughter proton, closed shell)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 1.736</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+5.29</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> (daughter neutron)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 1.257</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+2.19</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
